,title,link,text,language,family
0,Mizo culture - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mizo_Culture,"April 25, 2026 - Mizo is the official language of Mizoram, along with English. Mizo language, or Duhlián ṭawng, is a language belonging to the Sino-Tibetan family of languages, spoken natively by the Mizo people in Mizoram states of India and Chin State in Burma.",Ralte,Sino-Tibetan
1,Music of Tibet - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Music_of_Tibet,"May 6, 2026 - The music of Tibet reflects the cultural heritage of the trans-Himalayan region centered in Tibet, but also known wherever Indigenous Tibetan groups are found in Nepal, Bhutan, India and further abroad. The religious music of Tibet reflects the profound influence of Tibetan Buddhism on the culture.",Ralte,Sino-Tibetan
2,"Category:Ralte terms derived from Proto-Sino-Tibetan - Wiktionary, the free dictionary",https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Category:Ralte_terms_derived_from_Proto-Sino-Tibetan,Ralte terms that originate from Proto-Sino-Tibetan.,Ralte,Sino-Tibetan
3,Understanding the importance of Tibetan music,https://www.tibettravel.org/tibetan-culture/understanding-the-importance-of-tibetan-music.html,"May 6, 2025 - You will find that flutes and lutes combine with some percussion beats to create a soft aroma of music that is thought to resemble a constant communication link with the divine world, one that only ""perfect beings"" are able to compose. It is officially named Sino-Mongolian music and is heard in the streets during festivals and parties.",Ralte,Sino-Tibetan
4,Sino-Tibetan | Ethnologue Free,https://www.ethnologue.com/subgroup/236/,"Ralte ral, a language of India · Simte smt, a language of India · Sizang 4 · Chin, Siyin csy, a language of Myanmar · Gangte gnb, a language of India · Vaiphei vap, a language of India · Zo zom, a language of Myanmar · Thado 3 · Chin, Paite pck, a language of India ·",Ralte,Sino-Tibetan
5,"Tibetan ""Red Songs"" Series, Part 1: ""Laundry Song""",https://highpeakspureearth.com/tibetan-red-songs-series-part-1-laundry-song/,"March 16, 2022 - The song tells the familiar Socialist narrative of the army and the people being one. For the Sino-Tibetan relationship though, the song puts the Tibetans firmly in a position of subservience, as natives, full of gratitude for the help of the benevolent People’s Liberation Army.",Ralte,Sino-Tibetan
6,MUSIC IN TIBET | Facts and Details,https://factsanddetails.com/china/cat6/sub36/item206.html,Their songs and music are well-modulated in tone and the words fit well with the tunes.The areas inhabited by Tibetans boasts a great diversity of folk songs and dances. Some musical instruments were introduced from the interior of China.,Ralte,Sino-Tibetan
7,"Tibetan Music, Tibet Music and Songs, Traditional Tibetan Music",https://www.tibettravelexpert.com/tibetan-culture-tibetan-art/tibetan-music/,"November 27, 2016 - The characteristic of modern Tibetan songs is related to the special plateau natural scenery, vast blue sky with white clouds and numerous sheep and cows. The famous singers include Chinese singer Han Hong, Rongzhong Erjia, and Tseten Dolma and so on. Their songs introduce the incredible natural beauties and express how proud they feel about their hometown.",Ralte,Sino-Tibetan
8,Tibetan Dance & Music - YouTube,https://www.youtube.com/@tibetan_dance,"This channel is to introduce Tibetan dance, Tibetan songs, and Tibetan dance music to netizens around the world. Feel the elegance and beauty of ancient Tibetan culture, promote exchanges and enhance friendship.",Ralte,Sino-Tibetan
9,Tibetan traditional music Tibet - AstroNuclPhysics,https://astronuclphysics.info/HudbaTibet.htm,"The endless chanting of mantras by Tibetan monks takes place in a monotonous ""grunting"" voice with deep vibrations, which, however, has its melody and mystical impact. There is a peculiar peculiarity in the Tibetan vocal expression - an aliquot of biphonic throat singing .",Ralte,Sino-Tibetan
